1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,614
Sleep is an active process during which the brain sorts memories

2
00:00:04,614 --> 00:00:07,209
Clears waste built up during the day

3
00:00:07,209 --> 00:00:10,982
The night is split into repeating cycles of light sleep

4
00:00:10,982 --> 00:00:15,509
Deep sleep and dream sleep, each doing different work for the body

5
00:00:15,509 --> 00:00:19,106
Going without enough sleep makes it harder to concentrate

6
00:00:19,106 --> 00:00:23,082
Remember new facts and react quickly to what happens around you

7
00:00:23,082 --> 00:00:26,538
Over months and years, regular short sleep is linked

8
00:00:26,538 --> 00:00:29,927
With higher risks of heart problems and weight gain

9
00:00:29,927 --> 00:00:33,902
Keeping the same bedtime and wake-up time, even on weekends

10
00:00:33,902 --> 00:00:37,136
Helps the body clock settle into a steady rhythm

11
00:00:37,136 --> 00:00:40,774
Bright screens late in the evening can delay sleepiness

12
00:00:40,774 --> 00:00:44,345
Because light tells the brain that it is still daytime

13
00:00:44,345 --> 00:00:49,074
A cool, dark and quiet bedroom makes it easier to fall asleep

14
00:00:49,074 --> 00:00:51,555
To stay asleep through the night

15
00:00:51,555 --> 00:00:55,674
Caffeine blocks the signals that build up sleep pressure

16
00:00:55,674 --> 00:00:58,764
A late coffee can keep you awake for hours

17
00:00:58,764 --> 00:01:03,082
While you sleep, hormones that support growth and repair are released

18
00:01:03,082 --> 00:01:06,336
Which is why rest matters after hard physical effort

19
00:01:06,336 --> 00:01:10,374
To build a better routine, first fix your wake-up time

20
00:01:10,374 --> 00:01:14,636
Dim the lights early, and finally keep screens out of bed

21
00:01:14,636 --> 00:01:19,695
Sleep problems that last for weeks, such as loud snoring with daytime exhaustion

22
00:01:19,695 --> 00:01:21,845
Are worth discussing with a doctor

23
00:01:21,845 --> 00:01:25,329
Think of sleep like charging a phone overnight

24
00:01:25,329 --> 00:01:29,418
Skip it and you start the day running on a low battery

